      "content": "i mean i get that, but isn't it a bit unfair to keep a kid stuck in a failing school just to protect a \"system\" that isn't even working for them? it feels like the \"equal access\" argument is used to justify mediocrity for everyone instead of letting people actually succeed. isnt it more moral to prioritize an individual child's success over a budget line item?",
